The user wants to adjust the logo sizes. Looking at the screenshots:
1. The ChatGPT logo appears as thin horizontal lines (the SVG seems to not be rendering well or it's very small)
2. The Gemini logo appears to be showing but seems small

The user wants to resize the logos. Let me check the current CSS for `.demo__logo` and adjust the height.

Currently:
```css
.demo__logo {
  height: 28px;
  width: auto;
  display: block;
}
```

The ChatGPT SVG (`logo-chatgpt-noback.svg`) appears as white horizontal lines - that's because the SVG only has the icon (the circular/rotational shape in teal color `#74aa9c`), and it's quite small at 28px height. 

Looking more closely at the screenshots, the first one shows those thin horizontal lines which is the ChatGPT icon at its current small size, and the second screenshot appears to be showing the Gemini logo area, though it's hard to tell exactly what's rendering there.

I should just increase both logo sizes - bumping the ChatGPT icon up to around 36-40px to make it more visible, and adjusting the Gemini logo similarly so they're both more prominent in the navigation. The user said "로고 크기 조정" (logo size adjustment) and probably expects me to increase the logos to a reasonable larger size rather than ask for specifics. Looking at the ChatGPT logo's large SVG viewBox, it needs to be bigger than 28px to show the details properly—I'm thinking 40px would work well for both logos to keep them uniform and visually balanced.

I'm noticing something odd in the second screenshot though—it doesn't look like the Gemini logo I'd expect, more like a GROUP-D icon from the navigation. Let me check what's actually in those SVG files and just increase the logo height in the CSS to 40px to see if that resolves the visibility issue.

